
passwd    --> if you are executing this command as root, it will change password for root.
              if you are executing this command as ec2-user, it will change password for ec2-user


passwd viswa  --> it will change password for the account viswa.


passwd -S viswa   --> to check status of viswa password
chage -l viswa


| Status | Meaning         |
| ------ | --------------- |
| `PS`   | Password set    |
| `LK`   | Password locked |
| `NP`   | No password     |


passwd -l viswa    --> to lock password, user won't be login using username and password


passwd -u viswa     --> to unlock password


passwd -d viswa     --> to delete password


passwd -e viswa     --> Force a user to change password at next login


passwd -n 7 viswa   --> means the password cannot normally be changed again for 7 days.


passwd -x 90 viswa  --> means the password expires after 90 days.
chage -M 90 viswa


passwd -w 14 viswa  --> Warn the user 14 days before password expiration.


passwd -i 30 viswa  --> After the password expires, the account can become inactive after the specified number of days, depending on the system's account-aging implementation.


/etc/passwd  --> user account informatin is stored in this file
/etc/shadow  --> user account password is stored in this file


sudo -l   --> login as viswa, You can verify whether viswa has sudo permission





